# Project Rules

## Orientation
- `README.md` — what Chronicle is, how to run it
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — how it fits together and why
- `DEPLOYMENT.md` — Vercel + Fly.io, the MCP connector, the newsletter broadcast
- `env.example` — authoritative env var reference, with free-tier limits
- `TODO.md` — open items and known gaps

## Shape
- Next.js 14 App Router frontend (`frontend/`, port 3000) + FastAPI backend
  (`backend/`, port 8000). The frontend is **not** Vite; there is no `dist/`.
- Five-agent LangGraph pipeline in `agents/` + `orchestration/coordinator.py`,
  executed inline via asyncio (no ARQ worker in production).
- Two MCP surfaces — hosted (`backend/mcp_server.py`) and stdio (`mcp/`) — kept
  in sync by `backend/tests/test_mcp_parity.py`. Change one, change both.
- Three input modes: Type, Speak (Web Speech API), Picture (Tesseract.js OCR +
  GPT-4o vision via `POST /api/extract-image-text`).

## Conventions
- TypeScript strict mode; React function components with hooks
- FastAPI with Pydantic models
- Model names are `provider/model`; the prefix picks the SDK
  (`groq/`, `google/`, `anthropic/`, else OpenRouter). See `utils/llm_config.py`.

## Traps
- Don't point analyzer, insight and report at the same Google model — the free
  tier is 20 requests/day *per model* and the report stage 429s into an empty
  template.
- Never set `OPENROUTER_FALLBACK_MODEL` to a `:free` slug; those were retired
  and now 404 on every call, making the fallback silently useless.
- `NEWSLETTER_ADMIN_EMAILS` unset means every signed-in user can read and mail
  the subscriber list. It is a security control, not a convenience.
- `/mcp` returning 404 means "not configured", not "broken".
